/-!
# Finiteness of Selmer groups

Let `R` be a Dedekind domain with fraction field `K`, let `S` be a set of height one primes of
`R` and let `n` be a positive integer. `Mathlib.RingTheory.DedekindDomain.SelmerGroup` defines the
Selmer group `K⟮S, n⟯ ≤ Kˣ/(Kˣ)ⁿ` of the classes whose `v`-adic valuation is divisible by `n` for
all `v ∉ S`, and lists as `TODO`s the maps of the fundamental exact sequence
`1 → 𝒪_S(K)ˣ/(𝒪_S(K)ˣ)ⁿ → K⟮S, n⟯ → Cl(𝒪_S)[n] → 1` and the finiteness of `K⟮S, n⟯`. This file
constructs the first two maps, proves exactness in the middle and deduces finiteness from the
finiteness of `Cl(R)` and the finite generation of `Rˣ`. The `S`-class group is the class group of
the ring of `S`-integers `S.integer K`, a Dedekind domain whose primes are the `v ∉ S`
(`Mathlib.RingTheory.DedekindDomain.SInteger` and its mirror).

It also provides the bookkeeping for Selmer groups of extensions and of products: the Selmer group
of the fraction field of `B ⊇ R` relative to the primes above `S`, and the Selmer group of a
finite product of fields, transported along a decomposition of `Aˣ/(Aˣ)ⁿ`.

## Main definitions

* `IsDedekindDomain.selmerGroupAbove R B L S n`: the Selmer group of `L = Frac B` relative to the
  primes of `B` above `S`.
* `IsDedekindDomain.sUnitToSelmer` and `IsDedekindDomain.toSClassGroup`: the maps of the
  fundamental exact sequence.
* `IsDedekindDomain.selmerGroupPi` and `IsDedekindDomain.selmerGroupOfEquiv`: the Selmer group of
  a finite product of fields, and its transport along an isomorphism
  `Units.ModPow A n ≃* ((i : ι) → Units.ModPow (L i) n)`.

## Main statements

* `IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.toAdd_valuationOfNeZero_eq_neg_multiplicity`: the `v`-adic
  order of a unit that comes from `r : R` is minus the multiplicity of `v` in `(r)`.
* `IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.dvd_toAdd_valuationOfNeZero_map`: divisibility of adic
  orders transports along compatible embeddings of Dedekind domains.
* `IsDedekindDomain.toAdd_valuationOfNeZero_norm`: the `v`-adic order of the norm of `x` is the sum
  of the `w`-adic orders of `x` over the primes `w` above `v`, weighted by inertia degrees.
* `IsDedekindDomain.norm_mem_selmerGroup`: the norm maps `selmerGroupAbove` into `selmerGroup`.
* `IsDedekindDomain.map_algebraMap_mem_selmerGroupAbove_iff`: for a finite separable extension of
  degree prime to `n`, a class of `K` lies in `K⟮S, n⟯` iff its image lies in `selmerGroupAbove`.
* `IsDedekindDomain.selmerGroup_insert`: adjoining a prime `v = (r)` to `S` adjoins the class of
  `r`; `IsDedekindDomain.selmerGroup.fromUnit_surjective`: for trivial class group, `K⟮∅, n⟯` is
  the image of `Rˣ`.
* `IsDedekindDomain.selmerGroup_empty`, `IsDedekindDomain.selmerGroup_image_eq_range_sup_closure`,
  `IsDedekindDomain.selmerGroup_range_eq_range_sup_closure`: for trivial class group, `K⟮∅, n⟯`
  is the image of the units of `R`, and `K⟮{v i}, n⟯` for finitely many principal primes
  `v i = (r i)` is generated by it and the classes of the `r i`.
* `IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.valuationOfNeZeroMod_mk_eq_one_iff`: the Selmer condition at
  `v` on the class of `u` is the divisibility of the `v`-adic order of `u` by `n`.
* `IsDedekindDomain.isMulFG_sUnit`: the `S`-unit group is finitely generated, for finite `S` and
  finitely generated `Rˣ`.
* `IsDedekindDomain.ker_toSClassGroup`: exactness of the fundamental sequence in the middle.
* `IsDedekindDomain.finite_selmerGroup`: **`K⟮S, n⟯` is finite** if `Cl(R)` is finite, `Rˣ` is
  finitely generated, `S` is finite and `n ≠ 0`; `IsDedekindDomain.finite_selmerGroupAbove` for
  the primes above `S` in an extension and `IsDedekindDomain.finite_selmerGroupOfEquiv` for
  products.

## Implementation notes

`IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.valuationOfNeZeroMod_mk` is the computation rule for
`IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.valuationOfNeZeroMod` that Mathlib lacks (its definition has a
`TODO` about `Multiplicative`/`Additive` defeq abuse). The valuations of the factors of an étale
algebra are not derived from an `Algebra.Etale` hypothesis: the decomposition into fields is an
input (`AdjoinRoot.modPowEquivPiFactors` for `K[X] ⧸ (f)`).

Vendored from EllipticCurves (`EllipticCurves/Mathlib/SelmerGroup.lean`,
`EllipticCurves/Mathlib/FractionalIdeal.lean` and `EllipticCurves/Mathlib/Basic.lean`), for the
finiteness of the group `A(Σ, 2)` of the `x - T` descent; upstreaming candidates for Mathlib.
-/

